 "options": [{"text": "82", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}, {"text": "81", "added": false}, {"text": "83", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "weighted-average", "key_answer": "81"}, {"n": 11, "text": "A book was purchased for ₹1,020 and sold for ₹1,224. Find the profit percentage.", "options": [{"text": "18%", "added": false}, {"text": "19%", "added": false}, {"text": "21%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": "20%"}, {"n": 12, "text": "If at same rate of interest, in 2 years, the simple interest is ₹42 and compound interest is ₹49, then what is the principal (in ₹)?", "options": [{"text": "56", "added": false}, {"text": "67", "added": false}, {"text": "58", "added": false}, {"text": "63", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "si-ci-difference", "key_answer": "63"}, {"n": 13, "text": "Evaluate: (-9) - (-60) ÷ (-12) + (-4) × 8", "options": [{"text": "-45", "added": false}, {"text": "-49", "added": false}, {"text": "-48", "added": false}, {"text": "-46", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "-46"}, {"n": 14, "text": "Rupesh sold 153 chairs and had a gain equal to the selling price of 53 chairs. What is his profit percentage?", "options": [{"text": "53%", "added": false}, {"text": "63%", "added": false}, {"text": "58%", "added": false}, {"text": "48%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": "53%"}, {"n": 15, "text": "If the ratio of radius of the bases of two cylinders is 4 : 5 and the ratio of their heights is 5 : 2, then the ratio of their volumes is:", "options": [{"text": "4 : 3", "added": false}, {"text": "8 : 5", "added": false}, {"text": "5 : 3", "added": false}, {"text": "6 : 5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": "8 : 5"}, {"n": 16, "text": "A and B can finish a piece of work in 15 days and 20 days, respectively. If A and B work on alternate days, how many days will it take to complete the work (A starts the work)?", "options": [{"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "17.5", "added": false}, {"text": "17", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "alternate-days", "key_answer": "17"}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "26", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "early-late", "key_answer": "18"}, {"n": 18, "text": "The expenditure of Sudha is 125% more than her savings. If her expenditure decreases by 14% and savings increase by 38%, then by what percent does her income increase?", "options": [{"text": "5%", "added": false}, {"text": "4%", "added": false}, {"text": "3%", "added": false}, {"text": "2%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": "2%"}, {"n": 19, "text": "The average weight of Mohammad, Ashish and Kiran is 46 kg. If the average weight of Mohammad and Ashish be 40 kg and that of Ashish and Kiran be 42 kg, then the weight of Ashish (in kg) is:", "options": [{"text": "41", "added": false}, {"text": "26", "added": false}, {"text": "46", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "26"}, {"n": 20, "text": "What is the effective discount per cent if a shopkeeper offers a scheme, “Buy five and get three free”?", "options": [{"text": "37.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "41.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "33.8%", "added": false}, {"text": "35.5%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": "37.5%"}]}